P(\text{tie}) = 1 - P(\text{Amy wins}) - P(\text{Lily wins}) = 1 - \frac{3}{8} - \frac{3}{10}
\]
To subtract these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 8 and 10 is 40. So, we convert the fractions: \[
\frac{3}{8} = \frac{15}{40} \quad \text{and} \quad \frac{3}{10} = \frac{12}{40}
\]
Then, \[
P(\text{tie}) = 1 - \frac{15}{40} - \frac{12}{40} = 1 - \frac{27}{40} = \frac{40}{40} - \frac{27}{40} = \frac{13}{40}
\]
So the fraction of the time they tie is \(\frac{13}{40}\). </think> <answer> \(\frac{13}{40}\) </answer>

